  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of Members States to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the governance of labour migration and the labour market through a range of interventions related to policies, systems, institutional capacity building and services. Certain interventions are specifically targeted to reach migrants, as an identified vulnerable group; while other institutions serve all workers and employers. This will include guidance on matters related to fair recruitment and labour administration and governance. 
The broader institutional capacity building programme will enhance capacities and systems within the various bodies, to further enhance implementation. ILO will provide training, share international good practices, and provide inputs on systems and processes. 
This training is expected to be fully aligned or even integrated into the plans of the respective Departments in the MOL. The programme will actively encourage the participation of women in the training. For sustainability, the ILO office will seek to engage more local training institutions and experts, to the extent possible, and build the capacity of national institutions, including through ITC-ILO Turin.</narrative>
  </description>
